// name :
"P3988851221" "The Power to Control"
// // requiresfailedtext :
"P0" ""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BasiliskNote 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4249355776" "Note of Contact"
// DetailString :
"P3893793746" "You found this note on the body of Basilisk. It instructs him to input a series of numbers on one of the Static boxes in the underground. Doing so will put him in contact with someone named 'BV'."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LastWords 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1738642495" "Gorgon's Last Words"
// DetailString :
"P84044216" "Gorgon collapsed to the ground and looked up to you. He removed his mask and uttered these final words...<br><br><color DarkGray>So... Sinclair refused to let me go... he never could stand someone... going against his plans, having a will of their own. His eyes show no fear... but his plans... his movements, they show it all. He is terrified... terrified of losing control, losing his grasp on reality. Such a man... I could never continue to serve. I have... no regrets in my death... I can only... be happy that... I lived my last moments... free from him.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CockatriceFinal 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1179536365" "Cockatrice's Final Gasp"
// DetailString :
"P913560712" "Cockatrice gasped for air in his final moments, turning to you...<br><br><color DarkGray>Sinclair... He knew that my sister... would become just another tool for Praetoria... yet he led me to become this... I thought... I thought I could save her. I just... I just...</color><br><br>Cockatrice's eyes shut."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - TheFavoriteAssassinSouvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3023207740" "Basilisk's Mask"
// tDetailString :
"P664417689" "You took this mask from the body of a man named Basilisk. It reminds you of the work you did with Chimera in an experience you call...<br><br><color gold>The Power to Control</color><br><br>It all began when Praetor Sinclair's private group of assassins, Project Phoenix, went rogue and attempted to kill Praetor White. Sinclair requested your help in wiping out the group, saying that he would ensure that the people of Imperial knew you were wiping out a possible new threat. Of course, he would hide the fact that it was his own group that he lost control over. You went into the underground tunnels and finished off one of the men who tried to kill Praetor White. You also overheard threats from a woman named BV on the Static. You told this to Sinclair, who revealed that 'BV' was Belladonna Vetrano, one of the first to join Project Phoenix. He swore that she would be captured and that she would pay for her actions against him.<br><br>You went back into the tunnels to track down the next member of Project Phoenix, only to walk into an ambush set up by Belladonna. She was surprised when you showed up instead of Sinclair. You survived the ambush and went back to Sinclair, who already had plans set up for your next two actions.<br><br>The plan was simple, though a little different from what you were used to. You tracked down two more members of Project Phoenix - one located in the Syndicate, the other trying to reunite with his sister in the Seers. Sinclair was pleased that this all went down smoothly, though you did notice how controlling Sinclair was the entire time. Everything was perfectly set up for you each time: Sinclair went to great pains to ensure that there were no external variables. You can see why the other members of Project Phoenix wanted out - they became incredibly powerful, but very aspect of their lives was being controlled by Sinclair."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3505381489" "I will debrief you on the entirety of the situation, {HeroName}. I have my own personal and secretive strike force, codenamed <color yellow>Project Phoenix</color>.  Praetor White has his Powers Division, Marchand has the PPD, I have Project Phoenix. It is only fair that someone of my stature has their <i>own</i> force to rely upon. It was a small force, numbering only six in total. This was done to establish control and trust. However, something has gone wrong.<br><br>Earlier, an attempt was made on Praetor White's life by members of Project Phoenix, members who have gone rogue, obviously. Two members attacked him, only one made it out alive. I attempted to contact the other members of Project Phoenix, only to discover they have all fled. As you can see, there has been a small 'coup' within my group. The press is in an uproar about this, and Praetor White is... displeased. I must do what I can to keep my connection to all of this as secret as possible, which is why I am asking for your help in this."
// AcceptString :
"P3236871020" "My help? You can't do this yourself?"
// SendOffString :
"P3061544593" "It is a complicated matter, {HeroName}. I've made several deals with Praetor Tilman to hide my operatives from her seers. As you can imagine, this recent attempt on Praetor White's life has caused her no end of trouble. She is being pressured to explain how the assassins escaped the sight of her seers. Much as it displeases me, I am now indebted to her. In order to prevent her from revealing the truth, I must provide her with my assistance.<br><br>In the meantime, I'm relying upon you to <i>wipe out Project Phoenix</i>. I will spread the word that these assassins are part of a new group, looking to fill the growing void left by the Destroyers that you vanquished. Once more you will bear the role of the hero looking to take a stand and protect Praetoria. You will strike them down - of that I have no doubt - and my issue will be alleviated. And any of those who know about Project Phoenix will see what happens when my trust is betrayed.<br><br>I have tracked the member of Project Phoenix who attacked Praetor White. He is in the tunnels, recovering from his injuries. I must go deal with an errand for Tilman. It is up to you to wipe out this traitor before he can flee into the tunnels, lost forever to the darkness."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1523805050" "Eliminate a member of Project Phoenix."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3854893576" "You need to get that thing taken care of we talked about earlier."
// TaskTitle :
"P2147813044" "<color deepskyblue>The Power to Control</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1268269715" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: Control Lost</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3969791221" "The first member of Project Phoenix is in here somewhere, amongst the ghouls. You'll have to move to catch up with him."

