// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Static 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P3225872038" "Static"
// Description :
"P1083171198" "Find the Static Box to access the network"
// InteractBeginString :
"P1744097640" "Accessing the Static..."
// InteractInterruptedString :
"P535631865" "You have been interrupted."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P3343928950" "You've accessed the static!"
// InteractActionString :
"P2096386660" "Accessing..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1099465539" "You've opened up a link to the Static."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3420670888" "You put down Basilisk and encountered an odd message from a woman named BV."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3771511833" "Good, you're back. I've barely finished Tilman's request. You were able to put down Basilisk, I trust?<br><br>...BV? ...no, no, that's impossible. {HeroName}, what you are telling me is impossible. That person is supposed to be <i>dead</i>, many times over. The person you speak of is named <color yellow>Belladonna Vetrano</color>. She should be dead, {HeroName}. She should have died on her initial assignment - the assignement she never came back from - or from the numerous assassins I've sent after her, following her 'revival', you could say. But... her presence explains everything.<br><br>Belladonna was one of my most talented operatives within Project Phoenix. I saved her from her parents and offered her a life of riches, of fame, of power. I trained her, personally, taught her everything. She followed my commands and she benefitted from it time and again. It was perfect, {HeroName}. Up until she was sent to kill the woman named <color yellow>Vanessa DeVore</color>. I had believed she was killed by DeVore's powerful psychic powers. I was wrong. She betrayed me, {HeroName}. I gave her a meaningful life and she betrayed me by joining the Resistance, taken in by their lies. It simply showed me one thing: her faith in me was weak, fragile, easily swayed by simplistic words.<br><br>Since then, she and I have been in a constant battle. This latest move can only mean that she was able to poison others with her words. This situation has become more dire than I previously believed, {HeroName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P917625587" "The events that transpired with Belladonna are due to one thing and one thing alone, {HeroName}: control. I allowed Belladonna to do what she wished, despite the dangers that came with it. And now we are all paying for it. The worst thing about this situation is that I must leave it up to you to handle these things. You should understand, {HeroName}, the amount of trust I'm giving you. I have already begun to stream to the media that you are putting down this threat. I know what it is that you want and I fully intend to give it to you. <br><br>That, really, is what this is all about. Every person, no matter who they are, wants something. You can, as in your case, give it to them - for a price. Or you can cut them down, if what they want conflicts with your own plans. In Belladonna's case, it will be the latter. It is all about control and keeping it, {HeroName}."
// AcceptString :
"P344723394" "Alright, Praetor Sinclair. Do you have a lead on the next Project Phoenix member?"
// SendOffString :
"P1110123874" "That I do. There are four left, {HeroName}. One has been sighted again in the tunnels. Once more, I would deal with this myself, but Tilman requests that I deal with an urgent matter with her Seers and some other-wordly interference from psychics. As much as it pains me to do so, I must aid her. If I do not, then the balance she and I will be shattered and become unpredictable. And that, {HeroName}, is what leads to situations that we have now.<br><br>The person you're after is code-named Cockatrice. End him and in his last breaths make him wish that he never had the foolish idea to cross me."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3855366830" "Take down Cockatrice"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2842267476" "I cannot speak, {HeroName}. Tilman will be here shortly to discuss matters."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P441194777" "<color deepskyblue>Part Two: In Due Time</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P4061075985" "The smell of the Resistance is heavy in the air. It looks like Cockatrice has met up with his new allies."

