// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1539090218" "So, you saw Belladonna? I shouldn't be surprised that this was a trap. I taught her everything she knows about deception. I apologize, {HeroName}, that this happened to you. Her ingratitude knows no bounds.<br><br>I wonder, {HeroName}, what your reaction would be to someone who could be percieved as your savior. I told you about her parents, yes? They lived outside of Praetoria, in the wilds infested by the nightmarish creatures created by Hamidon. Her life was nothing but fear and chaos. The only thing that she and her parents could rely upon was never knowing what would happen next. She lived in pure and utter anarchy. I <i>rescued</i> her from that, {HeroName}. Her parents refused to let me take her, refused to let her daughter live a <i>better</i>, <i>safer</i> life. And so, I did what I had to in order to save her. She was barely nineteen when that happened; she remembers it well. And yet, here we are. She strikes against me, as if I am a monster, as if I am no better than the creatures that stalk her nightmares.<br><br> This, {HeroName}, is the reality that the Resistance would have us live. It is one that I intend to ensure never comes to fruition."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3665525035" "When someone becomes a member of Project Phoenix, they swear an oath. An oath to follow my every command. This is not because I am some... power freak, like White or Keyes. No, this is done because I know what is <i>best</i> for the members of Project Phoenix. I am, in many ways, their father. Every single member of Project Phoenix must give up their old life when they join, adopting the name that I give them. Belladonna was my Phoenix, until she betrayed me.<br><br>The current man we hunt is named Gorgon. He was once a member of the Syndicate, someone weak, someone petty, less than a man. I made him into something greater, into something legendary. But, like all the other members, he has succumbed to the lies of Belladonna. Like a son turned against a father by a traitorous sister.<br><br>I know the location of Gorgon. He has gone to meet with his former brother-in-arms, a brother he was supposed to have shed when he joined Project Phoenix. I have done you the honor of informing TPN that you believe this new group may be part of the Syndicate, and that you plan to storm one of their main offices with help from the fish named Riptide."
// AcceptString :
"P1166141501" "Sounds like you've gone and planned out everything, Sinclair."
// SendOffString :
"P1095812009" "That is the best way to handle things, {HeroName}. Careful planning, careful control. It prevents chaos, anarchy, and other things that can lead to... undesired consequences. Riptide will be waiting for you in the office building. Show Gorgon no mercy, {HeroName}, and make sure to bring down his brother. The man is now wanted for many crimes within Imperial City, thanks to our mutual friend, Praetor Tilman."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1308626667" "Bring down Gorgon and Adept Pham"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2075507311" "I would accompany you myself, {HeroName}, but things are beginning to get rather problematic with Praetor Tilman."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2858833547" "<color deepskyblue>Part Three: Stronger Than Family</color>"

